  "markdown": "# FastAPI OAuth2 Performance Overhead Analysis\n\n## Summary\nThe provided evidence does not contain performance benchmarking data, RPS metrics, or latency analysis for FastAPI 0.112.2 with `OAuth2PasswordBearer` [[cite:ref_0005]]. Consequently, it is impossible to quantify the overhead compared to unauthenticated endpoints based on the supplied documentation [[cite:ref_0001-ref_0008]].\n\n## Findings\n\n### Lack of Quantitative Performance Data\nThe documentation focuses exclusively on implementation mechanics and API schema generation rather than runtime performance characteristics [[cite:ref_0002]]. There are no tables, charts, or numerical values describing Requests Per Second (RPS) or latency differences between secured and unsecured routes [[cite:ref_0004]].\n\n### Focus on Functional Implementation\nAvailable resources detail how to configure `OAuth2PasswordBearer`, handle token extraction from headers, and integrate with OpenAPI/Swagger UI [[cite:ref_0006]]. The content explains the logical flow of authentication dependencies but omits any discussion of computational cost or throughput impact [[cite:ref_0007]].\n\n### Absence of Comparative Benchmarks\nNo experimental results comparing concurrent models (asyncio vs threading) or server configurations under load are present in the evidence [[cite:ref_0003]]. Without such comparative data, specific bottlenecks or overhead percentages cannot be identified [[cite:ref_0008]].\n\n## Limitations\n- No performance benchmarks or RPS data found.\n- No latency profiling or resource usage metrics available.\n- Documentation covers security setup, not performance optimization.",
